                          line 48 12304 744 20 base 14
                            span a 224 12306 28 16 link 477
                            text "In July 2012, WHATWG and " 48 12306 176 16 serif 16
                            text "W3C" 224 12306 28 16 serif 16 underline link 477
                            text " decided on a degree of separation. W3C will continue the HTML5 specification" 252 12306 508 16 serif 16
                          line 48 12324 744 20 base 14
                            text "work, focusing on a single definitive standard, which is considered a \"snapshot\" by WHATWG. The WHATWG" 48 12326 700 16 serif 16
                          line 48 12344 744 20 base 14
                            text "organization will continue its work with HTML5 as a \"Living Standard\". The concept of a living standard is that it is" 48 12346 744 16 serif 16
                          line 48 12364 744 20 base 14
                            text "never complete and is always being updated and improved. New features can be added but functionality will not" 48 12366 728 16 serif 16
                          line 48 12384 744 20 base 14
                            span span 128 12388 7 13
                            span span 148 12388 6 13
                            span span 128 12388 26 13
                            span a 128 12388 26 13 link 478
                            span sup 128 12388 26 13
                            text "be removed." 48 12386 80 16 serif 16
                            text "[" 128 12388 7 13 serif 13 underline link 478
                            text "53" 135 12388 13 13 serif 13 underline link 478
                            text "]" 148 12388 6 13 serif 13 underline link 478
