                      block p 8 22728 784 40
                        line 8 22728 784 20 base 14
                          span code 556 22730 64 16
                          text "The Frameset version includes everything in the Transitional version, as well as the " 8 22730 548 16 serif 16
                          text "frameset" 556 22730 64 16 mono 16
                          text " element (used instead of" 620 22730 168 16 serif 16
                        line 8 22748 784 20 base 14
                          span code 8 22750 32 16
                          span code 104 22750 40 16
                          text "body" 8 22750 32 16 mono 16
                          text ") and the " 40 22750 64 16 serif 16
                          text "frame" 104 22750 40 16 mono 16
                          text " element." 144 22750 60 16 serif 16
                    block section 8 22787 784 102
                      block div 8 22787 784 23
                        block h3 8 22787 784 23
                          line 8 22787 784 23 base 16
                            text "Frameset versus transitional" 8 22789 219 19 serif 19 bold
                      block p 8 22829 784 60
                        line 8 22829 784 20 base 14
                          text "In addition to the above transitional differences, the frameset specifications (whether XHTML 1.0 or HTML 4.01) specify a" 8 22831 780 16 serif 16
                        line 8 22849 784 20 base 14
                          span code 196 22851 64 16
                          span code 328 22851 32 16
                          span code 496 22851 40 16
                          span code 692 22851 64 16
                          text "different content model, with " 8 22851 188 16 serif 16
                          text "frameset" 196 22851 64 16 mono 16
                          text " replacing " 260 22851 68 16 serif 16
                          text "body" 328 22851 32 16 mono 16
                          text ", that contains either " 360 22851 136 16 serif 16
                          text "frame" 496 22851 40 16 mono 16
                          text " elements, or optionally " 536 22851 156 16 serif 16
                          text "noframes" 692 22851 64 16 mono 16
                          text " with" 756 22851 32 16 serif 16
                        line 8 22869 784 20 base 14
                          span code 20 22871 32 16
                          text "a " 8 22871 12 16 serif 16
                          text "body" 20 22871 32 16 mono 16
                          text "." 52 22871 4 16 serif 16
                    block section 8 22908 784 358
                      block div 8 22908 784 24
                        block h3 8 22908 784 24
                          line 8 22908 784 24 base 16
                            text "Summary of specification versions" 8 22910 266 19 serif 19 bold
                      block p 8 22950 784 200
                        line 8 22950 784 20 base 14
                          text "As this list demonstrates, the loose versions of the specification are maintained for legacy support. However, contrary to" 8 22952 776 16 serif 16
                        line 8 22970 784 20 base 14
                          text "popular misconceptions, the move to XHTML does not imply a removal of this legacy support. Rather the X in XML stands" 8 22972 780 16 serif 16
                        line 8 22990 784 20 base 14
                          text "for extensible and the W3C is modularizing the entire specification and opens it up to independent extensions. The" 8 22992 740 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23010 784 20 base 14
                          text "primary achievement in the move from XHTML 1.0 to XHTML 1.1 is the modularization of the entire specification. The strict" 8 23012 772 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23030 784 20 base 14
                          text "version of HTML is deployed in XHTML 1.1 through a set of modular extensions to the base XHTML 1.1 specification." 8 23032 732 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23050 784 20 base 14
                          text "Likewise, someone looking for the loose (transitional) or frameset specifications will find similar extended XHTML 1.1" 8 23052 760 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23070 784 20 base 14
                          text "support (much of it is contained in the legacy or frame modules). Modularization also allows for separate features to" 8 23072 756 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23090 784 20 base 14
                          text "develop on their own timetable. So for example, XHTML 1.1 will allow quicker migration to emerging XML standards such" 8 23092 772 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23110 784 20 base 14
                          span a 28 23112 52 16 link 647
                          span a 524 23112 48 16 link 648
                          text "as " 8 23112 20 16 serif 16
                          text "MathML" 28 23112 52 16 serif 16 underline link 647
                          text " (a presentational and semantic math language based on XML) and " 80 23112 444 16 serif 16
                          text "XForms" 524 23112 48 16 serif 16 underline link 648
                          text "—a new highly advanced" 572 23112 160 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23130 784 20 base 14
                          text "web-form technology to replace the existing HTML forms." 8 23132 372 16 serif 16
                      block p 8 23166 784 100
                        line 8 23166 784 20 base 14
                          text "In summary, the HTML 4 specification primarily reined in all the various HTML implementations into a single clearly" 8 23168 748 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23186 784 20 base 14
                          text "written specification based on SGML. XHTML 1.0, ported this specification, as is, to the new XML-defined specification." 8 23188 768 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23206 784 20 base 14
                          text "Next, XHTML 1.1 takes advantage of the extensible nature of XML and modularizes the whole specification. XHTML 2.0" 8 23208 756 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23226 784 20 base 14
                          text "was intended to be the first step in adding new features to the specification in a standards-body-based" 8 23228 672 16 serif 16
                        line 8 23246 784 20 base 14
                          span span 72 23251 7 13
                          span span 79 23251 78 13
                          span span 79 23251 78 13
                          span a 79 23251 78 13 link 649
                          span i 79 23251 78 13
                          span span 157 23251 6 13
                          span sup 72 23251 91 13
                          text "approach." 8 23248 64 16 serif 16
                          text "[" 72 23251 7 13 serif 13
                          text "AI-generated?" 79 23251 78 13 serif 13 italic underline link 649
                          text "]" 157 23251 6 13 serif 13
                  block section 8 23286 784 126
                    block div 8 23286 784 30
                      block h2 8 23286 784 30
                        line 8 23286 784 30 base 21
                          text "WHATWG HTML versus HTML5" 8 23289 288 24 serif 24 bold
                    block div 8 23336 784 20
                      line 8 23336 784 20 base 14
                        span span 140 23338 8 16
                        span a 92 23338 328 16 link 650
                        text "Main article: " 8 23338 84 16 serif 16
                        text "HTML §" 92 23338 48 16 serif 16 underline link 650
                        text " " 140 23338 8 16 serif 16 underline link 650
                        text "Transition of HTML publication to WHATWG" 148 23338 272 16 serif 16 underline link 650
                    block p 8 23372 784 40
                      line 8 23372 784 20 base 14
                        text "The HTML Living Standard, which is developed by WHATWG, is the official version, while W3C HTML5 is no longer" 8 23374 732 16 serif 16
                      line 8 23392 784 20 base 14
                        text "separate from WHATWG." 8 23394 152 16 serif 16
                  block section 8 23432 784 466
                    block div 8 23432 784 30
                      block h2 8 23432 784 30
                        line 8 23432 784 30 base 21
                          text "WYSIWYG editors" 8 23435 168 24 serif 24 bold
                    table table 8 23482 784 52
                      row-group tbody 10 23484 780 48
                        row tr 10 23484 780 48
                          cell td 10 23484 42 48
                            block div 11 23485 40 46
